<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Janatha Vimukthi Peramuna</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1965">1965</a>–present</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Janatha Vimukthi Peramuna (JVP), or People's Liberation Front, is a Marxist party in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a> founded in 1965 by Rohana Wijeweera. It led armed uprisings in 1971 and 1987–1989, both crushed by the state with heavy loss of life. Later entering parliamentary politics, it formed the core of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-peoples-power">National People's Power</a> alliance, whose leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anura-kumara-dissanayake">Anura Kumara Dissanayake</a> won the presidency in 2024.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/janatha-vimukthi-peramuna.jpg" alt="Janatha Vimukthi Peramuna" width="320" height="297" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: PLATEL · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Janatha_Vimukthi_Peramuna.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
